          = \frac{0.1454\ \text{N m}^{-1}}{1\times10^{-3}\,\text{m}}
          \approx 1.45\times10^{2}\ \text{Pa}
\]

Thus the air pressure at the nozzle must be about \(1.4\times10^{2}\) Pa higher than the water pressure. The answer closest to this value is 143.4 Pa.

