\[
k_{\mathrm B}=1.38\times10^{-23}\; \mathrm{J\,K^{-1}},\;
T=293\ \mathrm{K},\;
\eta=1.005\times10^{-3}\ \mathrm{Pa\,s},\;
D=4.0\times10^{-11}\ \mathrm{m^{2}\,s^{-1}},
\;
\nu=0.75\;\mathrm{cm^{3}\,g^{-1}}=7.5\times10^{-4}\ \mathrm{m^{3}\,kg^{-1}},
\;
N_A=6.022\times10^{23}\ \mathrm{mol^{-1}}
\]

gives  

\[
M \approx 5.1\times10^{5}\ \mathrm{g\,mol^{-1}}.
\]

Thus the molecular weight of serum globulin is about \(5.1\times10^{5}\) g mol\(^{-1}\).

